## Context
Author decision 2026-11-01 (brood report row 21, conception/2026-11-01-brood-harness-run.md): "Coder gazes; risky code adds a seat". Gaze stays in hunt Verify, run by the coder. When the diff touches gate, merge or review machinery, gaze's plan must include at least one seat from a family other than the producer's.

Evidence: PR #2149 (ticket 1403). The coder's own gaze was a self-only test-and-read and missed a blocking defect; the orchestrator's inline gaze with an OpenAI red-team seat found it: `git cherry` admitted a whitespace amend.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] skills/gaze/references/plan.md names the trigger paths and the requirement, in its one home
- [ ] When no other-family door is reachable the plan says so; the result stays valid (PR #2171). No gate refusal.
- [ ] `make lint` passes
